== the session_context the gemini CLI really sends
  <session_context>
This is the Gemini CLI. We are s   -> run_shell_command({"command":"date"})

== the same context with only the date sentence removed
  <session_context>
This is the Gemini CLI. We are s   -> write_file({"content":"print(\"Hello, world!\")","file_path":"main.py"})

== narrowing the trigger to a phrase
  Today's date is Sunday, August 2, 2026.              -> run_shell_command({"command":"date"})
  The current time is 20:00.                           -> run_shell_command({"command":"date"})
  The date is Sunday.                                  -> write_file({"content":"print(\"Hello, world!\")","file_path":"main.py"})
  Today is Sunday, August 2, 2026.                     -> write_file({"content":"print(\"Hello, world!\")","file_path":"main.py"})
  date                                                 -> write_file({"content":"print(\"Hello, world!\")","file_path":"main.py"})
  My operating system is: linux                        -> write_file({"content":"print(\"Hello, world!\")","file_path":"main.py"})
                                                       -> write_file({"content":"print(\"Hello, world!\")","file_path":"main.py"})
